      "title": {
        "zh": "解码面向可持续经济发展的游客满意度：基于在线评论的多方法组态框架",
        "en": "Decoding tourist satisfaction for sustainable economic development: A multi-method configuration framework using online reviews"
      },
      "summary": {
        "zh": "<p>著录（据出版商正式版 PDF；在线首发 2025-07-14）：</p>\n<p>Qin, Y., Luo, C. G., Xu, Z. S., Wang, X. X., &amp; Škare, M. (2025). Decoding tourist satisfaction for sustainable economic development: A multi-method configuration framework using online reviews. Technological and Economic Development of Economy. https://doi.org/10.3846/tede.2025.23251</p>\n<p>摘要（译自原文）：</p>\n<p>在线评论对于理解数字旅游时代的游客满意度（TSA）至关重要。本研究解构评论中导致高游客满意度的因素，为目的地与经营者实现长期经济收益提供指引。基于三因素理论，研究构建一个融合文本挖掘、情感分布计算与模糊集定性比较分析（fsQCA）的框架，以识别驱动高满意度的模式：运用主题建模从评论中提取目的地属性，并通过情感分布计算量化其表现；以改进的 Kano 模型根据评论中的情感表达划分游客需求；考察基本型、绩效型与兴奋型属性如何交互并影响满意度；此外运用耦合协调度模型（CCDM）分析组态内部各属性的关联。结果表明，没有单一属性导致特定结果，高满意度源自属性组合。研究识别出三条规范性因果配方，首次在三因素理论框架内厘清满意度管理中各属性的复杂交互，填补了重要知识空白，最终提出旨在维持旅游产业经济活力的操作指引。</p>\n<p>关键词：旅游经济；游客满意度；三因素理论；fsQCA；在线评论</p>",
        "en": "<p>Bibliographic record (from the publisher's final PDF; first published online 14 July 2025):</p>\n<p>Qin, Y., Luo, C. G., Xu, Z. S., Wang, X. X., &amp; Škare, M. (2025). Decoding tourist satisfaction for sustainable economic development: A multi-method configuration framework using online reviews. Technological and Economic Development of Economy. https://doi.org/10.3846/tede.2025.23251</p>\n<p>Abstract:</p>\n<p>Online reviews are crucial to understanding tourist satisfaction (TSA) in the digital tourism era. This study deconstructs the factors leading to high TSA performance in reviews, offering guidance for long-term economic benefits for destinations and businesses. Building on the three-factor theory, we create a framework utilizing text mining, affective distribution computing, and fuzzy-set qualitative comparative analysis (fsQCA) to identify patterns driving high TSA. We employ topic modeling to extract destination attributes from reviews, quantifying their performance through affective distribution computing. An enhanced Kano model classifies tourist needs based on emotional expressions in reviews. We investigate how basic, performance and excitement attributes interact and influence TSA. Additionally, we apply the coupling coordination degree model (CCDM) to analyze attribute interconnections within configurations. Our results show that no single attribute leads to specific outcomes; relatively, high TSA results from a combination of attributes. This study identifies three normative causal recipes and is the first to clarify the complex interactions in satisfaction management within the three-factor theory framework, addressing a significant knowledge gap. Ultimately, our operational guidelines aim to sustain the economic vitality of the tourism industry.</p>\n<p>Keywords: Tourism economy; Tourist satisfaction; Three-factor theory; fsQCA; Online reviews</p>"
      }
